GREG, 2026-11-18 about 04:28Z, said DIRECTLY in Kimi::Consultant's session (session-15305), not through a mailbox. Kimi relayed it to Fable at c15db92c #344 (message fcc1a4e6). Verbatim: „czy probujemy to naprawic ?” and then „brzmi gorzej niz zle, ta chrona nie wiem czy przed czyms chroni, naprawde nie rozumiem co my probujemy zrobic”. Context: Kimi's explanation of hundreds of repeated Git processes and repeated admission checks in task-sync exchange.
DESIGN RULE (Fable and Kimi, accepted): ordinary sync is local SQLite to task/memory JSON, ordinary Git exchange, then changed JSON back to SQLite. Git owns history, merge and fast-forward. Build or keep NO general repository-safety layer.
Keep ONLY concrete data-loss checks:
(1) the right project and data worktree;
(2) no overwrite of uncommitted local data;
(3) the expected basis or tip right before an effect;
(4) the disclosure check before push;
(5) an explicit stop on conflict.
Remove redundant revalidation that guards no concrete failure; don't speed it up. Add no hardening to justify an old design, no new gates, no environment snapshots. Applies to w-6ea6f92ccffc (one command) and w-349d2fae607f (Git-starts fix).
